ME>    Also have stolen a luckstone from Level 11 of the Gnomish Mines. Now
ME>I am extremely lucky, have extra luck and good luck does not run out on
ME>me (I blessed it with holy water on advice of the Oracle). Anybody have
ME>any idea what those terms mean? What is luck for?? And how does the game
ME>calculate at the altar whether there is reconciliation with your God?

You're playing in Wizard mode, aren't you? Nothing wrong with that,
except don't get too prideful when you ascend... Personally, I've never
ascended without Wizard mode.

Good luck increases your chance to hit, your damage, the chance to avoid
monsters' hits, traps etc. As a rule, it helps almost everything a
little.

Your god's liking of you depends on your alignment. For example, if
you're lawful, you shouldn't steal - otherwise your god gets pissed off.
And the gods don't like too much praying either.

ME>Magic-protection and perhaps other intrinsics such as displaced? And why

Displaced means that every (?) monster sees your character in a slightly
different position than you really are (basically it lowers your AC).
Magic-protection protects from magic :-) (e.g. protects somewhat against
dragons' breaths, wands zapped/potions thrown at you, magic traps etc.

ME>do people jump? (maybe I'll find that out later) And what's the

With the #jump-command you can jump over a few spaces, e.g. a trap or
water.

ME>difference between low boots and high boots and hard boots etc etc. Also

Not much, at least I don't know of any difference between those (hard
boots might have a better AC?). But boots of water walking, boots of
speed etc. do have their uses.

ME>attributes such as Wisdom and Charisma do exactly?

Strength increases your carrying capacity and damage.
Intelligence increases your spellcasting chances.
Wisdom increases your chance of resisting magic effects.
Dexterity lowers your AC, perhaps speeds you up.
Constitution increases your HP and regeneration speed.
Charisma affects the price shopkeepers give you, the chance of peaceful
monsters becoming aggressive (?), ...

Most of those are really only educated (I've played AD&D...) guesses.

